From 50f043b64b543bc47f30ae840061f5c206e24795 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <dev@infoverify.local>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 21:17:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] BVN Modification: require NIN number + a National ID card
 photo on every type

- Every one of the 8 modification types now also asks for NIN Number
  (new 'nin' input kind, same 11-digit validation as 'bvn') and a photo
  of the National ID card (new 'image' input kind) alongside the
  existing BVN/Enrollment Type/Bank Name fields - so an admin has proof
  of identity before re-keying anything.
- Image is sent as a data URL string (consistent with how PDFs are
  already stored inline via sealPII elsewhere in this file), validated
  server-side (must be a png/jpeg/webp data URL, capped at 7MB base64 -
  comfortably under express.json()'s existing 8mb limit) and embedded
  directly into the generated submission PDF via pdfkit's doc.image(),
  not printed as raw base64 text.
- Frontend: file-picker UI with client-side type/size checks (image
  files only, 4MB raw cap), a thumbnail preview, and a guard in
  prepare() that blocks opening the PIN dialog if a required photo is
  missing (a hidden native file input's own 'required' validation
  doesn't surface well once visually replaced by a custom label).

Verified: all 8 existing bvn-modification.service tests still pass
unchanged (vitest run, mocked Prisma - actually executed this time, not
just hand-reviewed). Frontend tsc + vite build both clean. Backend tsc
shows pre-existing stale-Prisma-client errors identical to
nin-modification.service.ts's (untouched, long-existing file) - not
something introduced by this change; the new nin/image-specific code
adds zero new errors beyond that baseline.
